--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,31 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Account and passkey settings
+
+After signing in, open **Account settings** in the header. The app verifies passwords
+with the existing Times identity service, then retains only the account identity in
+an HTTP-only server session. Passkeys are listed, renamed, and removed only for that
+session's account. Registration uses SimpleWebAuthn server verification and native
+browser WebAuthn APIs; accepted credentials are signaled on panel load and deletion
+where the browser supports the Signal API. Individual passkey names are local labels.
+
+Run on Node.js 22.13+ (Node.js 24 recommended) for built-in SQLite support. Set
+`ACCOUNT_DATABASE_PATH` to a SQLite file on a persistent volume (default:
+`data/accounts.sqlite`). All app processes must share that file; separate hosts need
+a shared database implementation. Persist the Astro session storage as well.
+Set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the public HTTPS origin behind a reverse proxy; the hostname
+is the RP ID and must remain stable. Localhost is supported for development.
+Provider names and compact icons are a snapshot of the
+[passkey-authenticator-aaguids registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids),
+used only as display hints. Unknown providers use a generic key icon.
+The snapshot keeps common provider icons small; other recognized providers use the
+same generic icon with their registered provider name.
+
+Passkey authentication at sign-in is outside this settings feature; passwords remain
+the sign-in method. Registration records are ready for a future authentication flow
+to verify signatures and update the persisted counter and last-used timestamp.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
